        "id": 94802,
        "name": "MigrantP",
        "username": "MigrantP",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/migrantp/{size}/1921_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-03-07T20:03:28.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I don't think you would need to print anything extra on the cards in order to accomplish what&nbsp;keitterman is talking about. Image recognition and augmented reality technology is at the point where the different SotM cards could be recognized uniquely already, I believe. Your app would just need to have reference images (or some representation thereof) of each card to detect them.</p><p>Games that are built from the ground up to harness the power of combining the digital and physical are really interesting; see <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/1613260297/golem-arcana\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">Golem Arcana</a>. Patching it onto an existing game is a bit more hit and miss, I think. It could work, but I have doubts that it could ever be super great.</p>",
